From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:13:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: open a D3DKMT adapter for a device that can share
 memory but has no LUID

DXVK makes its D3DKMT adapter, and so the D3DKMT device every shared
texture is opened, queried and described on, only from the Vulkan
device's LUID. Wine on iOS lists no display GPU, so win32u gives no
Vulkan device a LUID (DXGI falls back to "Adapter LUID 0"), DXVK had no
D3DKMT device, and with VK_KHR_external_memory_win32 now present
(patches/wine-unix 0034) a shared texture still failed:
"Failed to open shared D3DKMT handle", then "Failed to write shared
resource info for a texture", and the device that opens it finds nothing.

A device with VK_KHR_external_memory_win32 and no LUID now opens the
D3DKMT adapter with a zero LUID; Wine's D3DKMTOpenAdapterFromLuid gives
an adapter for any LUID, and DXVK uses the adapter only to make that
device. A device with a LUID is unchanged.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-vulkan-shared-texture-metal.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/dxvk/dxvk_adapter.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_adapter.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_adapter.cpp
index 96dfa5d..606a1e4 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_adapter.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_adapter.cpp
@@ -29,9 +29,13 @@ namespace dxvk {
     m_capabilities  (instance, handle, nullptr) {
     const auto& properties = m_capabilities.getProperties();
 
-    if (properties.vk11.deviceLUIDValid) {
+    // Wine on iOS lists no display GPU, so no Vulkan device has a LUID there;
+    // D3DKMT still opens an adapter for any LUID, and a texture or fence can
+    // only be shared through a D3DKMT device made on it.
+    if (properties.vk11.deviceLUIDValid || m_capabilities.getFeatures().khrExternalMemoryWin32) {
       D3DKMT_OPENADAPTERFROMLUID open = { };
-      memcpy(&open.AdapterLuid, properties.vk11.deviceLUID, sizeof(open.AdapterLuid));
+      if (properties.vk11.deviceLUIDValid)
+        memcpy(&open.AdapterLuid, properties.vk11.deviceLUID, sizeof(open.AdapterLuid));
 
       if (D3DKMTOpenAdapterFromLuid(&open))
         Logger::warn("Failed to open D3DKMT adapter");
